d but we would be in very  good shape right now compared to where  we are by mid March when the sporadic  stay at home orders started in some  states but not others the US had already  been seated with close to 4,000 cases of  coronavirus it was too late then to  really stop the spread it was especially  not going to happen when only some  states started stay at  home orders in the middle of March so  don't fall for the trumpets talking  point that there were no cases in  February and so it would have been crazy  to shut it down then they are right I  don't know of any president that with 15  cases would have demanded or asked 50  governors to shut things down but by  early March March 5 March 7 look at the  numbers for yourselves we had the data  that we needed to take it seriously and  Trump did not at that point in time  he'll brag he shut down travel from  China but but clearly at that point it  had gone outside of China to a  significant degree and we now have 33  million jobs lost but because of this  rolling patchwork of shutdowns in some  states and not in others we see some  states improving some worsening we still  have 2,500 deaths a day and FEMA and the  CDC believe it is possible that by June  1st we will actually be up to 3,000  deaths every single day it's been  mishandled let's be accurate in our  criticism of how it's been mishandled  but it has been dramatically mishandled  and not only are we seeing a human toll  we are also seeing an optional economic  toll we were going to have an economic  impact but we could have you know  grinned and bared it for 60 days  starting March 5th and we would be in  much better shape right now
 

